# orchestration/local.env.example -- copy to `orchestration/local.env` and fill in.
#
# THE FILE THIS IS AN EXAMPLE OF IS GIT-IGNORED ON PURPOSE. It says whose programme
# THIS POD is running -- which project, which GCP project, which machines are
# ours, which Slack channel the launchers post to -- and a fact about one pod is
# not a fact about the repository. The scripts in `orchestration/scripts/` name
# none of these (task P-4 of `toptal/ai-avatar-research`); every one of them
# reads this file through `orch-env.sh`, in a subshell, taking only the keys
# below. The ENVIRONMENT WINS: a value already set is never overwritten by this
# file, so `ORCH_GCP_PROJECT=x orchestration/scripts/status.sh` works anywhere.
#
# THIS FILE IS DOCUMENTATION AND NOTHING READS IT. Every line below is a comment
# on purpose: copied unedited, it sets nothing, and every script that needs a key
# without a default says which one rather than running on somebody else's values.
#
# scripts/bootstrap-repo.sh (in the kit; every first message runs it) writes the
# real file: project and machine prefix. pod-setup.sh adds the Slack channel once
# #maestro-<session> exists; vm-probe.sh --project adds the GCP project.
# `status.sh`'s first row prints what it read and from which file.

# ORCH_PROJECT: the programme's short name, in the launchers' prompts and the
# status row. No default.
#ORCH_PROJECT=viewstock

# ORCH_GCP_PROJECT: the GCP project our machines are in; `status.sh`,
# `state-check.sh` and the launchers' gate list its instances, `fetch-secrets.sh`
# reads its Secret Manager. `CLOUDSDK_CORE_PROJECT`, when set, still wins in the
# status and state checks. No default: a guessed project reports somebody else's
# machines as ours, or none of ours at all.
#ORCH_GCP_PROJECT=toptal-ai-research-staging

# ORCH_VM_PREFIX: the name prefix that makes a machine OURS -- the only machines
# a launcher refuses to start over, and the prefix of the secrets
# `fetch-secrets.sh` reads. A fixed string, not a pattern. No default.
#ORCH_VM_PREFIX=viewstock-

# ORCH_SLACK_CHANNEL: the id of the session's channel `#maestro-<session>`,
# which the launchers post to and tell the orchestrator to post to -- never
# anybody's self-DM: the pod's `slack` CLI posts as the owner. No default: a
# guessed channel is a batch plan posted into somebody else's session.
# `pod-setup.sh` fills it in by resolving the channel's name once it exists.
#ORCH_SLACK_CHANNEL=C0123456789

# ORCH_REPO_NAME: owner/name of this repository, in the status row and
# land-branch.sh's opening line. Default: read from `git remote get-url origin`.
#ORCH_REPO_NAME=toptal/ai-viewstock-research

# ORCH_MODEL_ORCHESTRATOR, ORCH_MODEL_FALLBACK, ORCH_MODEL_WORKER: the launchers'
# first model, the one they fall back to when it is refused for usage credits
# (and the reset drill's), and spawn-worker.sh's when the caller names none.
# Defaults are the owner's decision (docs/STATE.md section 5, docs/OPERATING.md
# section 2) and are safe on any pod; pass `--model` explicitly to override once.
#ORCH_MODEL_ORCHESTRATOR=claude-fable-5-1
#ORCH_MODEL_FALLBACK=claude-opus-5
#ORCH_MODEL_WORKER=claude-opus-5-5
